  "body": "## Finding Description  \nThe GaugeV2 contract's reward accrual mechanism fails to properly account for emissions when the total supply of staked tokens is zero, resulting in reward tokens being transferred to the contract but never becoming claimable by users. The issue arises in the reward distribution logic where rewards are accrued proportionally to the total supply. Specifically, in the [`rewardPerToken`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/74c2b93e8a4796c1d41e1fbaa07e40b426944c44/ve33/contracts/GaugeV2.sol#L180-L186) function, if _totalSupply == 0, it returns the stored value without adding the time-based accrual (lastTimeRewardApplicable() - lastUpdateTime) * rewardRate * 1e18 / _totalSupply. Meanwhile, the updateReward modifier, called during user interactions or notifications, advances lastUpdateTime to the current applicable time regardless of supply. This skips reward accumulation for empty periods, and subsequent notifyRewardAmount calls only consider leftovers from the remaining time after the advanced lastUpdateTime, leaving previously skipped rewards unaccounted for and trapped in the contract's balance. The highest impact scenario occurs when the gauge remains empty for an entire reward duration (one week), causing the full epoch's emissions to become permanently unclaimable.\n\nIn the[ `rewardPerToken`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/74c2b93e8a4796c1d41e1fbaa07e40b426944c44/ve33/contracts/GaugeV2.sol#L180-L186) function of GaugeV2, when _totalSupply == 0, the function skips the addition of new accrued rewards and returns only the stored value, while `lastUpdateTime` is still updated forward in the updateReward modifier, preventing retroactive accrual of skipped periods.\n[https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/74c2b93e8a4796c1d41e1fbaa07e40b426944c44/ve33/contracts/GaugeV2.sol#L180-L186](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/74c2b93e8a4796c1d41e1fbaa07e40b426944c44/ve33/contracts/GaugeV2.sol#L180-L186)\n```solidity\nfunction rewardPerToken() public view returns (uint256) {\n    if (_totalSupply == 0) {\n        return rewardPerTokenStored;\n    } else {\n        return rewardPerTokenStored + (lastTimeRewardApplicable() - lastUpdateTime) * rewardRate * 1e18 / _totalSupply; \n    }\n}\n```\n\n1. Users call withdraw or withdrawAll to remove all staked tokens from the gauge, setting _totalSupply to zero.  \n2. Time passes without any deposits, and during this period, notifyRewardAmount\n may be called by the distribution contract to add new rewards, but accrual is skipped in rewardPerToken\n due to zero supply while lastUpdateTime advances.  \n3. Even after new deposits occur and users interact (e.g., via `deposit`), the skipped rewards remain unaccrued and unclaimable, as future calculations do not retroactively include the empty period's emissions.\n\n## Impact:  \nEntire epochs of reward emissions can become permanently stuck in the contract, leading to protocol fund loss without recovery, with higher impact in low-liquidity gauges that frequently empty, potentially wasting significant token allocations over time.\n## Recommendation  \nTo prevent skipped accruals, modify the updateReward modifier and rewardPerToken to not advance lastUpdateTime when _totalSupply == 0, ensuring that future accruals capture the full pending period once supply is non-zero. Alternatively, track undistributed rewards separately and add them to future rates, but the simplest fix is to conditionally update time only when accrual occurs.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## poc\n```c\nforge test --match-test submissionValidity -vvv\n```\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {GaugeV2} from \"../contracts/GaugeV2.sol\";\n\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title C4PoC\n * @notice A complete deployment of the CL contract suite\n * @dev All available variables are showcased in the commented\n *      storage slots of the contract.\n */\n\n// Deployed contracts\n// ProxyAdmin public proxyAdmin;\n// PermissionsRegistry public permissionsRegistry;\n// VeArtProxyUpgradeable public veArtProxy;\n// TokenHandler public tokenHandler;\n\n// HYBR public hybr;\n// RewardHYBR public rewardHybr;\n// GrowthHYBR public gHybr;\n// VotingEscrow public votingEscrow;\n\n// GaugeFactory public gaugeFactory;\n// GaugeFactoryCL public gaugeFactoryCL;\n\n// PairFactory public thenaFiFactory;\n\n// GaugeManager public gaugeManager;\n// BribeFactoryV3 public bribeFactoryV3;\n\n// MinterUpgradeable public minter;\n// RewardsDistributor public rewardsDistributor;\n\n// VoterV3 public voter;\n\n// address public deployer;\n\n// Imported contracts\n// address public clPoolFactory;\n// address public clPoolImplementation;\n// address public clNonfungiblePositionManager;\n// address public clNftPositionDescriptor;\n// address public clSwapRouter;\n// address public clQuoter;\n// address public clSwapFeeModule;\n// address public clUnstakedFeeModule;\n// address public clProtocolFeeModule;\n\n// Administrative Addresses\n// address public team = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n// address public poolFactoryOwner = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n// address public feeManager = 0xf39Fd6e51aad88F6F4ce6aB8827279cffFb92266;\n\ncontract MockERC20 is ERC20 {\n    constructor(string memory name, string memory symbol) ERC20(name, symbol) {}\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external { _mint(to, amount); }\n}\n\ncontract MockRHYBR {\n    IERC20 public token;\n    constructor(address token_) { token = IERC20(token_); }\n    function depostionEmissionsToken(uint256) external {}\n    function redeemFor(uint256 amount, uint8, address to) external {\n        // Pull from Gauge using its approval and send to `to`\n        token.transferFrom(msg.sender, to, amount);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {}\n\n    // PoC: Rewards notified during zero supply are permanently unclaimable\n    function test_GaugeV2_ZeroSupplyRewardsStuck_submissionValidity() external {\n        // Setup mocks\n        MockERC20 reward = new MockERC20(\"Reward\", \"RWD\");\n        MockERC20 lp = new MockERC20(\"LP\", \"LP\");\n        MockRHYBR rhybr = new MockRHYBR(address(reward));\n\n        // Deploy GaugeV2 with DISTRIBUTION set to this test contract\n        GaugeV2 gauge = new GaugeV2(\n            address(reward),\n            address(rhybr),\n            address(0), // VE not needed for this PoC\n            address(lp),\n            address(this), // DISTRIBUTION = test contract\n            address(0), // internal bribe\n            address(0), // external bribe\n            false // isForPair\n        );\n\n        // Fund distribution and approve the gauge to pull rewards\n        uint256 rewardAmount = 1000e18;\n        reward.mint(address(this), rewardAmount);\n        reward.approve(address(gauge), rewardAmount);\n\n        // Notify rewards while total supply is zero\n        gauge.notifyRewardAmount(address(reward), rewardAmount);\n        uint256 duration = gauge.DURATION();\n        uint256 finish = gauge.periodFinish();\n\n        // Half the epoch elapses with zero supply (no accrual recorded)\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + duration / 2);\n\n        // Deposit after half of the period has passed\n        uint256 depositAmount = 1e18;\n        lp.mint(address(this), depositAmount);\n        lp.approve(address(gauge), depositAmount);\n        gauge.deposit(depositAmount);\n\n        // Advance to period finish and compute expected post-deposit accrual\n        uint256 remaining = finish - block.timestamp;\n        assertEq(remaining, duration / 2, \"remaining should be half the duration\");\n        uint256 rate = gauge.rewardRate();\n        vm.warp(finish);\n\n        uint256 earnedBefore = gauge.earned(address(this));\n        uint256 expected = rate * remaining; // Only accrual after deposit\n        assertEq(earnedBefore, expected, \"accrual skips zero-supply interval\");\n\n        // Claim rewards; MockRHYBR pulls tokens out of the gauge using approval\n        gauge.getReward(0);\n        assertEq(reward.balanceOf(address(this)), expected, \"claimed equals post-deposit accrual\");\n\n        // Leftover rewards remain stuck in the gauge\n        uint256 stuck = reward.balanceOf(address(gauge));\n        assertEq(stuck, rewardAmount - expected, \"pre-deposit rewards are stuck\");\n\n        // No further accrual after period end\n        vm.warp(finish + 1);\n        assertEq(gauge.earned(address(this)), 0, \"no accrual after period finish\");\n    }\n}\n```",
